    "retainable": false,
    "identity": 1,
    "diligenceRequirements": "Whitehats must notify 1inch Security immediately upon initiating any rescue action; provide full written disclosure of the vulnerability, rescue methodology, and all addresses used within 24 hours; execute and adhere to an NDA until 1inch confirms the vulnerability has been patched and publicly disclosed; not be sanctioned or owned or controlled by sanctioned persons; cooperate with sanctions and AML screening before bounty disbursement; and, for rescues over USD 250,000 gross exploited value, provide reasonable cooperation with a forensic investigation conducted by an independent incident-response firm engaged by 1inch. Excludes blackhats, accomplices, and former insiders within the 12-month look-back. Where 1inch has reasonable doubt as to compliance, 1inch may require additional information sufficient to verify identity, jurisdiction, and beneficial ownership as a precondition to bounty disbursement."
